.TH NAMTOR-DAEMON 8 "2026-09-16" "namtor 0.1.0" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
namtor\-daemon \- Nam-tor infrared face authentication daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B namtor daemon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B namtor daemon
owns the infrared camera and emitter, runs face detection, liveness
detection and template matching, and serves authentication requests on
.IR /run/namtor/auth.sock .
It is started by systemd and takes no arguments beyond the
.B daemon
subcommand. Inference runs in a separate sandboxed worker process: the
daemon re-execs its own executable as
.B namtor worker
(resolved through
.IR /proc/self/exe ),
which applies seccomp and Landlock to itself before serving. Daemon and
worker are the same file but never the same process — the sandbox is the
privilege boundary.
.PP
The daemon runs as the unprivileged
.I namtor
user with an empty capability bounding set. Raw camera frames, embeddings
and match scores never leave the daemon: the authentication socket carries
only a pass/fail verdict, and the management interface on the system bus
carries only coarse progress and guidance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/namtor/auth.sock
PAM authentication socket, group
.IR namtor\-auth .
.TP
.I /var/lib/namtor/templates
Encrypted enrolled face templates.
.TP
.I /var/lib/namtor/models
ONNX models used for detection, recognition and presentation-attack
detection.
.TP
.I /usr/share/namtor/install-manifest.toml
Install manifest consulted at startup to resolve installed paths.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NAMTOR_WORKER_BIN
Fallback path to the executable re-exec'd as the sandboxed inference
worker, used only when
.I /proc/self/exe
cannot be read. Set by the shipped systemd unit to
.IR /usr/bin/namtor .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown, or
.B \-\-help
/
.B \-\-version
printed.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failed.
.TP
.B 2
Unrecognised command-line argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR namtor\-cli (1),
.BR pam_namtor (8)
.SH NOTES
.B namtor
is a single multi-call executable:
.BR "namtor daemon" ,
.BR "namtor worker" ,
.BR "namtor cli " ...
and
.B namtor emitter-off
.I DEVICE
are all the same file. The PAM module
.RB ( pam_namtor.so )
and the enrolment wizard
.RB ( namtor\-enroll\-wizard )
are deliberately separate artifacts.
